    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="cde79828-93ba-5569-9f49-3f0ee24f67c4" activityNameId="8c112a62-3065-5221-8f17-298dbbca5f68" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Round wood, softwood, under bark, u=70%, holzpur, at forest road</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Round wood, softwood, under bark, u=70%, holzpur, at forest road
The volume refers to the wood not including the bark. The economic allocation of the process to the three coproducts roundwood, residual wood and industrial wood is done according to specific data on the volume shares and prices of the products. Data on the fuel use for building machines, power sawing and passenger cars are specific for the Korporation Giswil, which delivers the wood to Walter Küng AG for the production of holzpur elements.;
UUID: 4c3ab272-4446-3321-a03d-8707066c01ec
Includes motormanual processes for thinning and final cutting as well as transport of the products to the nearest forest road.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at the Korporation Giswil in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4c3ab272-4446-3321-a03d-8707066c01ec.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
